<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FlexiPage xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>decorate</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;Tenders IQR went live for CCG on Tuesday, September 20&lt;em&gt;th&lt;/em&gt;! Recordings from the training sessions are available on the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://intel.sharepoint.com/sites/MeetComp/SitePages/Tenders-IQR-Training.aspx&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Tenders IQR Training SharePoint.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Did you know&lt;/strong&gt;…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;You are now able to access the deal in My Deals by simply clicking on the Deals ID hyperlink in IQR for each quote line!&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The End Customer list in IQR is not populated with accounts from Salesforce and is instead a list of end customers for which the OEM has previously submitted a tender. Reminder: Check the End Customer drop down list before accepting a Write In End Customer entry. If the End Customer already exists, select the drop-down option, and save the change.&amp;nbsp;More information is available by visiting the &lt;a href=&quot;https://salescrm.intel.com/intel-quote-request-home/tenders-iqr-home/tenders-iqr-overview/tenders-iqr-overview-customer-data-governance/&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Customer Data Governance&lt;/a&gt; section on the IQR Training website.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;The next release is scheduled for WW30.4. This will include a few new features including a Sales Dashboard, the ability for full access users to edit and save external reports, and account executives will be able to see the Approved ECAP for quotes they are named on.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To help you quickly access the information you need, this homepage can be customized. The intent of the sections below is for you to select list views that contain quote lines pending your review, quote lines that will be auto-rejected, and quotes where there is an AE listed but no Opportunity linked. To get started, go to the Quote Lines tab and clone or create the list views that you want to select on the home page. View the&lt;a href=&quot;https://salescrm.intel.com/training-and-help/salescrm-functionality/creating-new-views/#lexhowtocreatenewviews&quot; rel=&quot;noopener noreferrer&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Sales CRM Training&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;if you need help customizing your list views. After you’ve created your list views, select them from the lists in the sections below. If you have questions, reach out to your Regional Lead.&lt;/p&gt;</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>flexipage:richText</componentName>
                <identifier>flexipage_richText</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
